## Context

Owner, 2026-11-17: he cannot tell if worker sessions are idle or working, and handily made it worse than bare Claude Code; it needs a new design. Orchestrator design (.orchestrator/design/session-state/DESIGN.md, section 6, decided 2026-11-17): herdr screen detection is the only session-state authority, with a hook reporter built in basicly; handily-board keeps no second state machine.

Order (decided): the reporter lands in herdr, the owner checks it, then the Orchestrator tells this session to start. Not before.

## Scope (from the handily code check of 2026-11-17)

Remove from mods/handily-board, with their tests, README sections and docs/mocks.md and docs/design.md sections:
- own-session turn state (working, waiting, idle, no turn), the Session frame-title state, the classic.Stop background lists and the Esc restore: hooks/background.ts, the state parts of hooks/session.ts and hooks/progress.ts (isWorking and published background), the classic.Stop, turn.start and turn.complete state handling in hooks/register.tsx (about lines 1938 and 1978); retires the rules of handily-uht4tq;
- the this machine tab: hooks/agents-json.ts (the 15 s claude agents poll), hooks/sessions.ts, hooks/machine.tsx, hooks/cards.ts, and /board machine;
- the Inbox: hooks/waits.ts and its store key session:<id> (retires handily-fwkt.8.28);
- the 3-second needs-you rule (NEEDS_YOU_AFTER_MS in hooks/agents.ts) and the desktop notice it fires (register.tsx about 1261);
- the status-line writer (register.tsx about 1163) and the band state marks and waiting rows (hooks/band.ts).
Keep: subagent rows with their tool, age and fold, minus their needs-you mark.
Dropped from handily-d75xdi: items 4 and 5 (simple-view state marks, slow mark).
